> 
> I understand that the obvious solution is to learn the VI keys. But I 
> always mistake 'j' and 'k' or 'h' and 'j' so I very often move in wrong 
> ways.
> 
> Is there a way to make the arrow keys usable? Some kind of key mapping 
> or such a magic?

Doing so would restrict your movement to orthogonal only. You don't want 
to do that. There are situations where running diagonally achieves 
something you can't do running orthogonally. Running away from nasties 
is one. Looting Croesus without stepping on a mine is another.

The best way I've heard of learning the vi keys is this: Put your four 
fingers directly on the h,j,k,l keys. Now your leftmost finger goes 
left, your rightmost finger goes right, and j (which looks a bit like a 
down arrow) goes down. It helps that my keyboard has a dimple on j to 
keep my hand aligned with the correct keys.

